    "title": "History of 16 Seed vs 1 Seed in March Madness - Bleacher Nation",
    "text": "March Madness has arrived, and you are scrambling to figure out your bracket. You think you can just pencil in the No. 1 seeds in round 2, but has a No. 16 ever beat a No. 1 seed in the NCAA Tournament? Let’s look at the history of the 1 vs 16 seed game in college basketball’s biggest David vs Goliath matchups. How Many Times Has No. 16 Beat a No. 1 Seed? A No. 16 seed has beaten a No. 1 seed just 2 times in NCAA Tournament history. No. 1 seeds have a 158-2 record in the matchup heading into the 2026 tournament. Get a $250 deposit bonus on BN Fantasy! When was the Last Time a 16 Beat a 1? (Fairleigh Dickinson upset Purdue in 2023 in a shocker. Photo: Adam Cairns-USA TODAY Sports) In 2023, No. 16 Fairleigh Dickinson beat No. 1 seed Purdue 63-58. The Boilermakers were 29-5 entering the game with star center Zach Edey leading the way. Purdue was just 5-26 from three in the game and had 16 turnovers in the loss. Sean Moore led Fairleigh Dickinson with 19 points. March Madness No. 16 vs No. 1 History (UMBC was the first No. 16 to upset a No. 1. Photo: Jeremy Brevard-USA TODAY Sports) Heading into the 2018 tournament, there had never been an upset of a No. 1 seed by a No. 16. That all changed when UMBC beat Virginia 74-54 on March 16, 2018. Virginia was 31-2 entering the game and the top overall seed in the whole tourney. UMBC shot 50% from three, and the Retrievers were in control the whole game. Virginia was just 4-22 from three. Take a look at the only two upsets of a No. 1 seed in the NCAA Tournament. The matchup began back in 1985 when the tournament expanded to 64 teams. The tournament expanded again to 68 teams in 2011. From 1985 until 2018, the No. 1 seeds held an undefeated record against No. 16 seeds. Year16 Upsets 1Score2023Fairleigh Dickinson def. Purdue63-582018UMBC def. Virginia74-54 2026 NCAA Tournament 1 vs 16 Matchups Will we see a No. 16 pull off a huge upset this season? Take a look at the schedule for the No. 1 vs No. 16 matchups in the 2026 March Madness Tournament. The top seeds in the tournament this year are Duke, Michigan, Arizona, and Florida. 1 vs 16DateTime (ET)1 Duke vs 16 Sienna3/192:50 PM1 Michigan vs 16 UMBC / Howard3/197:10 PM1 Arizona vs 16 Long Island3/201:35 PM1 Florida vs 16 Prairie View / Lehigh3/209:25 PM Responsible Gaming Resources written by Sam hails from Grandville, Michigan. He has a rich sports background, including playing baseball at Central Michigan before covering high school sports and working with the Orlando Magic. He earned his broadcasting/journalism degree from Central Michigan University and was a member of the 2010 MAC Championship baseball team. Sam developed his expertise while working with Betsperts, Bleacher Nation, and 4for4 in various areas such as writing, social media, betting research, and business development. He's a big fan of the NBA, NFL, and MLB, highly interested in data and statistics.",
